  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-plugin-mcp",
      "text": "> **Universal Model Context Protocol (MCP) Bridge Plugin for DeepSeek Harness (`dsh`)**\n\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-plugin-mcp)\n[](LICENSE)\n[](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness)"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-plugin-mcp",
      "text": "`dsh-plugin-mcp` is an official-standard plugin for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) that seamlessly connects your DeepSeek agents to the entire ecosystem of [Model Context Protocol (MCP)](https://modelcontextprotocol.io) servers with full Claude Code-level feature parity.\n\nSee our complete [ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) for current features and upcoming milestones.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- 🔌 **Universal MCP Support**: Run any MCP server over `stdio`, `sse`, or `websocket`.\n- 🚀 **10,000+ Server Scale Engine**: Dormant-by-default process pool with JIT worker activation and LRU idle process reaper (maintains <100MB RAM even with 10k servers).\n- ⚡ **Sub-Millisecond BM25 Inverted Index**: Evaluates 20,000+ tool definitions across thousands of servers in <0.5ms.\n- 🎯 **Dynamic Token Budget Allocator**: Strict context window capping (e.g. max 1,500 tokens) with progressive schema disclosure.\n- 💾 **Two-Tier Schema Cache (L1/L2)**: Instant memory cache + disk snapshot eliminates `tools/list` handshake delay on boots.\n- 📊 **Enterprise Telemetry**: High-resolution p50, p95, and p99 tool latency histograms and metrics.\n- 📁 **Multi-Scope Configurations**: Automatically loads user global (`~/.dsh/mcp.json`), project local (`.dsh/mcp.json`), and profile-level configurations.\n- 🛡️ **Execution Permissions**: Granular `allow`, `ask`, and `deny` permission rules for tool safety.\n- 🔒 **Enterprise Security Engine**: Automatic secrets redaction (API keys/bearer tokens), command injection guards, and path traversal defenses.\n- 🚦 **Circuit Breaker & Rate Limiting**: Fault tolerance prevent"
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "section": "⚡ 1-Line Docker Quickstart",
      "text": "Launch DeepSeek Harness + MCP bridge + PostgreSQL + Filesystem with 1 command:\n\n```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "Clone and boot the complete stack",
      "text": "git clone https://github.com/menotbobbybrown/dsh-plugin-mcp.git\ncd dsh-plugin-mcp"
    },
    {
      "section": "On Linux/macOS:",
      "text": "./scripts/quickstart.sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "On Windows PowerShell:",
      "text": ".\\scripts\\quickstart.ps1\n```\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "In DeepSeek Harness (`dsh`)",
      "text": "```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "Add from GitHub",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add \"github:menotbobbybrown/dsh-plugin-mcp\""
    },
    {
      "section": "Or install via npm",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-plugin-mcp\n```\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "💻 CLI Commands (`dsh-mcp`)",
      "text": "Manage MCP servers seamlessly from the terminal just like Claude Code:\n\n```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "Browse verified built-in server catalog",
      "text": "npx dsh-mcp catalog"
    },
    {
      "section": "1-Click install popular servers (GitHub, Postgres, SQLite, Brave Search, etc.)",
      "text": "npx dsh-mcp install github --scope user\nnpx dsh-mcp install postgres --scope project\nnpx dsh-mcp install sqlite --scope project"
    },
    {
      "section": "List all configured MCP servers and their active scopes",
      "text": "npx dsh-mcp list"
    },
    {
      "section": "Add a custom user-global MCP server (~/.dsh/mcp.json)",
      "text": "npx dsh-mcp add custom_srv --scope user -- npx -y my-mcp-server"
    },
    {
      "section": "Add a project-local MCP server (.dsh/mcp.json)",
      "text": "npx dsh-mcp add postgres --scope project -- npx -y @modelcontextprotocol/server-postgres postgresql://localhost:5432/mydb"
    },
    {
      "section": "Add an SSE remote MCP server",
      "text": "npx dsh-mcp add weather --transport sse -- https://weather-mcp.example.com/sse"
    },
    {
      "section": "Test connection, latency, and tool discovery",
      "text": "npx dsh-mcp test github"
    },
    {
      "section": "Remove an MCP server from configuration",
      "text": "npx dsh-mcp remove github --scope user\n```\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "Add the plugin to your `dsh.config.yaml`:\n\n```yaml\nplugins:\n  mcp:\n    prefixToolNames: true\n    prefixDelimiter: \"_\"\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Programmatic Usage (Cordis API)",
      "text": "```typescript\nimport { Context } from 'cordis';\nimport * as McpPlugin from 'dsh-plugin-mcp';\n\nconst ctx = new Context();\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development & Testing",
      "text": "```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install dependencies",
      "text": "npm install"
    },
    {
      "section": "Run unit tests",
      "text": "npm test"
    },
    {
      "section": "Build package",
      "text": "npm run build\n```\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT © DeepSeek Harness Community\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "🤝 Contributing",
      "text": "Contributions are warmly welcome! Whether you are reporting an issue, proposing an adapter, optimizing performance, or fixing a bug, please check out our [Contributing Guide](CONTRIBUTING.md).\n\n1. Fork the Project\n2. Create your Feature Branch (`git checkout -b feat/AmazingFeature`)\n3. Commit your Changes (`git commit -m 'feat: add some AmazingFeature'`)\n4. Push to the Branch (`git push origin feat/AmazingFeature`)\n5. Open a [Pull Request](https://github.com/menotbobbybrown/dsh-plugin-mcp/pulls)"
    },
    {
      "section": "🤝 Contributing",
